---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="About page for NyankoTools, covering what the service is, who operates it, and how to get in touch."
>
  <h1 class="mb-2 text-2xl font-bold">About</h1>
  <p class="mb-8 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
    An overview of NyankoTools and who operates it.
  </p>

  <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-8 text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-300">
    <section>
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">About the Service</h2>
      <p>
        NyankoTools (nyankotools.com) is a free, browser-only toolkit covering
        everyday tools like JSON formatting and Base64 conversion, plus careful
        support for Japanese-specific text processing such as kana and
        full-width/half-width conversion. No account is required, and nothing
        you type is ever sent to our servers.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">Operator</h2>
      <p>
        The Site is operated by an individual. We don't publish the operator's
        name, but you can reach us via our official X account below, or through
        the
        <a
          href="/en/contact/"
          class="text-blue-700 underline hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
        >
          contact form
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">Official X</h2>
      <p>
        We announce new tools and maintenance updates on our official X account.
      </p>
      <a
        href="https://x.com/nyankotools"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="text-blue-700 underline hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
      >
        @nyankotools
      </a>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">Open-Source Licenses</h2>
      <p>
        The HEIC to JPG Converter uses the LGPL-3.0 licensed open-source library
        &quot;heic-to&quot; and the &quot;libheif&quot; library it bundles. The
        full license texts are available for{' '}
        <a
          href="/licenses/heic-to-LICENSE.txt"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="text-blue-700 underline hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
        >
          heic-to (LGPL-3.0)
        </a>{' '}
        and{' '}
        <a
          href="/licenses/libheif-COPYING.txt"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="text-blue-700 underline hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
        >
          libheif (LGPL-3.0)
        </a>
        . libheif: Copyright (c) 2017-2020 Struktur AG, Copyright (c) 2017-2026
        Dirk Farin. The source code can be obtained from{' '}
        <a
          href="https://github.com/hoppergee/heic-to"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="text-blue-700 underline hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
        >
          heic-to on GitHub
        </a>{' '}
        and{' '}
        <a
          href="https://github.com/strukturag/libheif"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="text-blue-700 underline hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
        >
          libheif on GitHub
        </a>
        . These libraries are used unmodified.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        The Video &amp; Audio Converter uses the MPL-2.0 licensed open-source
        libraries &quot;mediabunny&quot; and
        &quot;@mediabunny/mp3-encoder&quot;. MP3 output includes a WebAssembly
        build of the LGPL-licensed LAME MP3 Encoder (
        <a
          href="https://lame.sourceforge.io/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="text-blue-700 underline hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
        >
          lame.sourceforge.io
        </a>
        ). Licenses:{' '}
        <a
          href="/licenses/mediabunny-LICENSE.txt"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="text-blue-700 underline hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
        >
          mediabunny (MPL-2.0)
        </a>
        ,{' '}
        <a
          href="/licenses/mediabunny-mp3-encoder-LICENSE.txt"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="text-blue-700 underline hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
        >
          @mediabunny/mp3-encoder (MPL-2.0)
        </a>{' '}
        and{' '}
        <a
          href="/licenses/lame-license.txt"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="text-blue-700 underline hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
        >
          LAME
        </a>
        . The source code is available on{' '}
        <a
          href="https://github.com/Vanilagy/mediabunny"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="text-blue-700 underline hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
        >
          mediabunny on GitHub
        </a>
        . These libraries are used unmodified.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">Related Pages</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-6">
        <li>
          <a
            href="/en/contact/"
            class="text-blue-700 underline hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
          >
            Contact
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="/en/updates/"
            class="text-blue-700 underline hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
          >
            Updates
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="/en/faq/"
            class="text-blue-700 underline hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
          >
            FAQ
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="/en/privacy-policy/"
            class="text-blue-700 underline hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
          >
            Privacy Policy
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="/en/terms-of-service/"
            class="text-blue-700 underline hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
          >
            Terms of Service
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
